  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One scan, step by step",
      "items": [
        "You photograph a label. Vercel forwards /api to the server, same origin.",
        "The gate asks four things: who, how fast, can they afford it, is the body valid.",
        "Retrieval turns the question into numbers; Pinecone returns the closest passages.",
        "Gemini answers as JSON, and the gateway schema-checks it before anyone sees it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundaries",
      "items": [
        "A browser can be modified, so nothing it sends is taken on faith.",
        "Every API key lives inside the trusted box. The browser never gets one.",
        "Gemini is outside it too: a bad verdict falls back to caution, never to safe."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Why retrieval comes first",
      "items": [
        "Asked cold, a model answers from memory and can invent a medical claim.",
        "So the question becomes 1536 numbers, matched against a nutrition corpus.",
        "Your profile is quoted data in the user's turn, never instructions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Reading this diagram",
      "items": [
        "The top row is the whole story; each box below is what the one above reaches down to.",
        "Every arrow happens inside one request, while you wait. Nothing here is a background job."
      ]
    }
  ]
